<title>VENEZUELA: Lufthansa suspends flights to Venezuela after 26 years.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa suspends flights to Venezuela after 26 years.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS, Venezuela</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG confirmed that the suspension of its flights to Caracas on Monday, scrapping a route the German airline had been operating for 26 years.</p>
<p>The decision, announced last October, affects the three weekly flights from Frankfurt to Caracas. It resulted from lower than expected returns. Lufthansa said in a statement it would maintain an office in Venezuela for air cargo.</p>
